            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates prepare rocky soil for driveway paving in Mendon, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates excavates large boulders and loose topsoil using heavy hydraulic excavators. The subgrade is backfilled with a 6-to-8 inch layer of processed gravel containing crushed stone and binder fines, which is compacted to maximum density using a vibratory roller. This dense aggregate base prevents rocky subsoil from pushing through the surface course during winter frost-heaving in Mendon.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What hardscaping materials are best for lakefront properties in Mendon, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates recommends permeable paver systems, thermal bluestone, and natural New England fieldstone for lakefront hardscapes around Lake Nipmuc. Permeable pavers allow rainwater to filter back into the subsoil naturally, reducing runoff into local water bodies while providing a frost-resistant, non-slip surface for patios, walkways, and pool decks.</p>
